# Private key material, anywhere in the tree — added 2026-09-20.
#
# A P-256 signing key for BudgetApp's SSO was found here untracked and UNIGNORED,
# which in a public repository is one `git add .` from publishing it. It had never
# been committed, so nothing was exposed — but the near miss is the reason for a
# rule rather than a habit. simtrader needs no private keys of its own: it verifies
# BudgetApp's tokens against the PUBLIC half at BUDGETAPP_JWKS_URL, and its own
# secrets go in workers/.dev.vars or `wrangler secret put`.
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12

# Workers local dev secrets (never commit)
workers/.dev.vars
# Names our Cloudflare account, KV/Hyperdrive resources and IdP hostnames — public repo.
# Copy workers/wrangler.toml.example and keep the real file on the dev machines only.
workers/wrangler.toml
# Local `wrangler dev` state — holds whatever KV your dev session wrote, including session tokens
workers/.wrangler/

# Claude Code local settings (may contain secrets)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Node
workers/node_modules/
